        "senate_pages": [],
        "first_page": "                DEADLINES FOR\n      NEW VOTER REGISTRATIONS AND\n CHANGES TO EXISTING VOTER REGISTRATIONS\n         (if you have recently moved)\n            for the November 3, 2026\n                 General Election\n\n                      REGISTRATION IN PERSON\nIn person registration and changes to existing voter registrations for the General\nElection closes at 6:00 p.m. on October 23, 2026. All persons wishing to vote in the\nNovember 3, 2026 General Election must have attained the age of 18 on or before the\nfirst Tuesday following the first Monday in November of this year.\n\n\n               REGISTRATION AT DMV OR ONLINE\n                              In person registration at DMV\n                      or Online www.ne.gov/go/NEreg2vote for the\n                          General Election is October 16, 2026.\n\n\n                         REGISTRATION BY MAIL\nMail in registrations for the General Election shall be postmarked no later than\nOctober 16, 2026. If registering to vote for the first time, you will want to include a copy\nof identification such as your Nebraska driver’s license to your registration application.\nThe only form which may be used shall be the official registration form provided by the\nCounty Clerk/Election Commissioner or the Secretary of State.\nhttps://www.votercheck.necvr.ne.gov\n\n\n          VOTER REGISTRATIONS SHOULD BE MAILED TO:\n           1111 13th Street Suite 1 Aurora NE 68818\n                       https://hamiltoncountyne.gov\n\n                                                                      Jill M. DeMers\n                                                                 Hamilton County Clerk\n"
      },
